\section{From the planar aperture to the triswale and helix chirality}

Now take the three circle planes as equatorial planes whose origins are initially coplanar, with their twist axes separated by $120^\circ$. A cooperative signed twist deforms the central planar aperture into a threefold saddle, here called the \emph{triswale}. Near its center, the lowest smooth threefold mode has the form
\begin{equation}
z(\rho,\phi)
= A_3\rho^3\cos\!\bigl(3(\phi-\phi_0)\bigr)+\mathcal O(\rho^4).
\label{eq:triswale}
\end{equation}
The coefficient $A_3$ is preferable to Gaussian curvature at the central point because the canonical cubic saddle has vanishing quadratic curvature there. $A_3$ is therefore a candidate signed order parameter for the threefold deformation.

Let $\theta_4$ denote the helix tangent angle measured from the axial/common-normal direction. For a circular helix of radius $a$ and signed pitch per turn $p$,
\begin{equation}
\tan\theta_4=\frac{2\pi a}{p},
\qquad
p=2\pi a\cot\theta_4.
\label{eq:helixpitch}
\end{equation}
The complement $\delta=\pi/2-\theta_4$ is the angle measured from the transverse/coplane direction. This explicit reference convention is essential because $\theta_4$ has changed meaning across SAT/\HsH history.\mcite{PROV:THETA4-DRIFT-20260920}

A minimal signed helix variable is therefore
\begin{equation}
s\equiv\frac{p}{2\pi a}=\cot\theta_4.
\label{eq:signeds}
\end{equation}
In the ideal zero-thickness limit,
\begin{equation}
s>0 \leftrightarrow \text{one chirality},\qquad
s<0 \leftrightarrow \text{the opposite chirality},\qquad
s=0 \leftrightarrow \text{zero pitch / densely wound continuous limit}.
\label{eq:chirality}
\end{equation}
If the triswale response is smooth and mirror-odd near the crossover, then
\begin{equation}
A_3(s)=-A_3(-s),
\qquad
A_3(s)=\kappa_3 s+\mathcal O(s^3),
\label{eq:A3odd}
\end{equation}
for some geometry-dependent coefficient $\kappa_3$. Equation~\eqref{eq:A3odd} is a testable ansatz, not yet an exact contact solution.

Finite filament thickness complicates the literal $s=0$ limit because neighboring turns can contact before the centerline pitch reaches zero. The correct finite-thickness quantity is the minimum surface-to-surface rung clearance, which must be computed from the tube geometry rather than silently identified with the axial pitch. Contact, fusion, and topological reconnection are also distinct events.

The important structural possibility is nonetheless clear:
\begin{equation}
\text{triswale sign}
\longleftrightarrow
\text{helix chirality}
\longleftrightarrow
\text{signed pitch / rung structure},
\end{equation}
with the chirality-neutral state coincident, in the idealized limit, with the discrete-to-continuous crossover.

\section{Local twist, global toroidal closure, and the Forest}

The pieces can now be assembled without claiming more than has been shown.

A Forest edge may carry a Hagalaz relation $\Hrel_{ij}$. Its rotational component $Q_{ij}$ can contain local twist information. A closed chain of such edges carries a holonomy $Q_\gamma$ as in Eq.~\eqref{eq:holonomy}. If the large-scale geometry is toroidal, repeated local rotations may close only for discrete winding sectors. Schematically,
\begin{equation}
\text{local frame step}
\longrightarrow
Q_\gamma
\longrightarrow
\text{global winding/holonomy sector}.
\label{eq:localglobal}
\end{equation}

This is the precise place where statements such as ``the number of twists in the donut'' can become mathematics: one must define the local step, the path, the composition law, and the closure condition. If a winding number $N$ is obtained, a further rule would still be required before identifying $N$ with a particle count or any cosmological census. The relation
\begin{equation}
N_{\mathrm{particles}}\stackrel{?}{=}f(N_{\mathrm{winding}})
\end{equation}
is a research question, not a consequence of toroidal closure alone.

The possible role of $B$ is then sharper. Rather than treating $B$ as an isolated fitted number, ask whether it is the invariant normalization of the local threefold relation that is repeatedly composed by Hagalaz. If so, local threefold geometry could feed a global closure law. The correct program is therefore
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
\text{threefold packing}
\to
\text{tangent invariant}
\to
B
\to
\text{signed twist}
\to
Q_{ij}
\to
Q_\gamma
\to
\text{global chirality/closure}
}
\label{eq:program}
\end{equation}
with every arrow independently derived or rejected.

This is also where the information principle re-enters. If SAT nonlocality is a real transverse worldtube transmission, then the same native geometry that determines $Q_{ij}$ and $Q_\gamma$ should also determine which vertices in the Forest are physically adjacent for information transfer. Geometry and information are not separate ontologies: the information path is a path in the physical geometry.

\section{Three-state proxies: $uud/udd$ and chirality imbalance}

A three-circle model naturally invites a binary label on each of three local strands. If $u$ and $d$ are used only as provisional labels for two opposite local twist states, then
\begin{equation}
uud \sim (+,+,-),
\qquad
udd \sim (+,-,-),
\end{equation}
with net signed local chirality
\begin{equation}
q_\chi(uud)=+1,
\qquad
q_\chi(udd)=-1.
\end{equation}
A globally achiral geometry would make these mirror sectors symmetric at this level. A global toroidal chirality $\chi_U$ permits an odd coupling of the schematic form
\begin{equation}
E_\chi=\lambda\,\chi_U q_\chi+\cdots.
\label{eq:chiral_coupling}
\end{equation}
This has the correct symmetry to split the two proxy sectors, but it is \emph{not} a derivation of the proton--neutron mass difference, nor does it establish that the labels correspond to Standard Model quarks. That mapping would require an independent particle-physics derivation.

Likewise, a matter--antimatter asymmetry would require more than a signed geometric preference. The relevant question would be whether the full dynamics contains the necessary symmetry violation and number-changing/non-equilibrium structure. The geometry may supply an order parameter or bias; it does not by itself supply baryogenesis.

\section{What is actually connected, and what is not yet connected}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.30\textwidth} >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.24\textwidth} >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.34\textwidth}}
\toprule
Statement & Current status & What would strengthen or kill it \\
\midrule
Information about an actual referent requires a realized physical ancestry & Foundational principle; formalized by channel/processing language & Clarify edge cases involving global constraints and quantum causal structure; no purely formal counterexample can work unless it carries a physical anchor somewhere \\
Mathematical post-processing cannot manufacture referential information absent in its physical inputs & Standard data-processing structure & Track all background variables $K$ rather than pretending ``pure math'' has no inputs \\
Hagalaz tuple $(\Delta c,\sigma,Q)$ is a coherent relation representation & Narrowly multiply verified project result & Recover/define the actual Hagalaz dynamics and internal state $\mathcal P$ \\
Three-circle tangent step is $2\pi/3$ & Exact Euclidean geometry & None; interpretation is the open part \\
$B=3/(4\pi)=1/(2\Delta_3)$ & Exact identity under the declared two-sided normalization & Derive the factor of two from geometry rather than choose it post hoc \\
Triswale sign tracks helix chirality & Candidate symmetry mapping & Solve the three-boundary contact/deformation problem and compute $A_3(s)$ \\
Chirality crossover coincides with discrete/continuous crossover & Exact only in an idealized zero-thickness parameterization & Replace pitch by true finite-tube clearance and distinguish contact from fusion \\
Local twist determines global torus winding/closure & Structurally plausible through holonomy & Define the actual toroidal path, edge law, and closure sector; compute $Q_\gamma$ \\
Particle count follows torus winding count & Speculative & Supply a forced occupancy/quantization map $f(N)$ \\
Worldtube-transverse transmission explains Bell correlations & Foundational SAT hypothesis, not demonstrated & Build an explicit causal/statistical model reproducing Bell/CHSH behavior while respecting operational no-signalling \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\section{Immediate research program}

The Forest becomes useful only if it constrains the next calculations. The immediate sequence is:

\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.6em]
\item \textbf{Define native locality.} Specify the SAT/\HsH worldtube adjacency relation $\sim_W$ and the degrees of freedom that actually transmit a physical difference transverse to ordinary time propagation.
